ial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y-7x,\\,y(1)=3\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $Δy$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{6}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $$ | $$ | $\\,?\\,$ |" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304880 1113 #uuid "56338bc4-f0b6-5400-8fc1-d56b70cb9bd1" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304880 1145 "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=3,$ we fill $y=3$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2y-7x \\\\  & =2(3)-7(1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{6}$ |" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304882 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304883 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304884 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304885 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304886 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1041 "selection" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304885 13194139534711 true] [17592186304881 1110 #uuid "0a6ee4c6-aa0c-5764-9ae8-375c27cd1345" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304882 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304882 1103 #edb/ref 17