 =2(-1)(3) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =3+(-3) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈0.$" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304889 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304890 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304891 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304892 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304893 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1041 "selection" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304891 13194139534711 true] [17592186304888 1110 #uuid "aef02c17-9352-5e12-beca-5d1d85015aec" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304889 1034 "2" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534711 true] [17592186304889 1111 #uuid "0d70ccee-a7c3-55f1-bf21-d871bff2060e" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304890 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534711 true] [17592186304890 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534711 true] [17592186304890 1111 #uuid